    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0043" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.939/243: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-15T12:00:00+08:00">August 15,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 15—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. My 154, August 10, 3 p.m.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d55-f1"/> Commissioner of
                    Customs has just informed me by telephone that Superintendent of Customs has
                    received necessary authorization from Peiping and that embargo on lambskins and
                    lamb plates with hair not exceeding 25mm. in length has been removed effective
                    immediately.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Chungking, Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
